WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
A screen fills with letters. Your assignment is to find the first target.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:13.000
The first target appears. You report it. More letters rush past.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:20.000
A second target appears within the next fraction of a second.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:27.000
You may miss the second, even while correctly reporting the first.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:34.000
Researchers call this task-dependent gap the attentional blink. It isn't a literal blink of the eye.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:40.000
What appeared, what you reported, and why you missed it are three different questions. Follow the evidence.
